vice_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T21:30:57.412Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVM8fzFXNq34yxwkeAqL", "thinking_duration_ms": 23109}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 1, "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgVM8gGsCNEwATdRdFB4e", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Estimated by hand: I worked out mean costs and buffer levels for each plan without simulating it. Each order lands 2 days later, so I lined each plan up against the forecast demand for its arrival day.\n\n1. **Daily ordering (plans 0, 2, 3, 5, 7):** each pays the 50 ordering fee about 28 times, about 1,400 in total. They differ only in quantity relative to forecast: 0 is about 0.85×, 5 is 1.0×, 3 is about 1.15×, 2 is about 1.25×, and 7 is about 1.3× for product 0 and 1.1× for product 1. Mean demand is 1.046× forecast. So plan 0 runs short every day, and 2 and 7 build a surplus of product 0 that spoils after 4 days at a loss of 12 per unit.\n2. **Ordering every 2 days (plans 4, 6):** 14 orders cost 700 in fees. The extra holding cost for the second day's stock is about 17 a day, against a fee saving of 25 a day.\n   - Plan 4 orders about 1.11× forecast for product 0 and about 1.03× for product 1.\n   - Plan 6 orders about 1.2× and about 1.11×.\n   - For product 0, a shortage costs 16 (lost margin 9 plus penalty 7) and spoilage costs 12, so the right level is only slightly above mean demand.\n   - For product 1, both costs are 8, so the right level is about mean demand.\n   - Plan 4 is closer to both targets. Plan 6 will lose more to spoilage.\n3. **Ordering every 3 days (plan 1):** it orders at the same levels as plan 4, but its total cost is about 8 a day higher. Leftovers from a 3-day batch have only one day of shelf life left, so more spoils. It also gets close to the 248-unit warehouse limit (for example, 120 + 110 units in one delivery).\n\nPlan 4 is my best guess for the highest expected profit, with plans 6 and 1 behind it."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4385, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2305, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4385}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T21:31:04.856Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVM8fzFXNq34yxwkeAqL"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01HfMFKvn9RWMzFyuefuTLbD", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgVM8gGsCNEwATdRdFB4e", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01HfMFKvn9RWMzFyuefuTLbD", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0.01, 0.17, 0.02, 0.04, 0.48, 0.02, 0.24, 0.02]}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4385, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2305, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4385}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_ge